<title>USA: Northwest sells South End facilities.</title>
<headline>Northwest sells South End facilities.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northwest Pipeline Corp said Friday it has completed the sale of a 77.7 percent interest in its South End facilities to Enron Corp's Transwestern Pipeline Co.</p>
<p>In a separate statement, Enron said it paid $21.9 for the interest in the 33-mile, 30-inch pipeline system which extends from Ignacio, Colo., to Blanco, N.M.</p>
<p>As a part of the sale, Northwest said, it is retaining 23.81 billion Btu of south flow and some 213.0 billon Btu of northbound capacity for its existing system-wide customers. The pipeline is owned by Williams Cos Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
